--- new packaged udev rule (ADR-009, VID:PID) — NOT yet installed ---
# Apple iBridge Touch Bar (T1/T2) — seat assignment + user access.
#
# ADR 009: match by USB VID:PID 05ac:8600, NOT by product name, so every
# name variant is covered:
#   - "Apple Inc. iBridge Touchpad"          (MBP14,2 bench)
#   - "Apple Inc. Apple T1 Controller Touchpad" (Seborider PR #1)
#   - "Apple Inc. Touch Bar Display Touchpad" (T2)
#   - "MacBookPro17,1 Touch Bar" / "Mac14,7 Touch Bar"
# Matching by name chases new variants forever; VID:PID is stable across
# T1/T2 Touch Bar hardware.
#
# This is the upstream fix for Seborider PR #1 (see
# docs/seborider-pr1-issue.md).

# Assign the Touch Bar digitizer to seat-touchbar so the engine's
# libinput seat-touchbar context enumerates it.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8600", \
  ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-touchbar"

# Grant the active console user seat-style access (replaces a hardcoded
# group requirement).
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8600", \
  TAG+="uaccess"--- digitizer udevadm info (PRE-deploy; expect seat0, no uaccess) ---
